// SOUNDNESS QUEUE row owned_return_from_ref_param_keeps_loan_refused (tier 3, `refuses`). Feature-interaction audit 2026-09-26, cluster index-clone-keeps-borrow: a returned value of an owned type T (no lifetime) from a fn taking &T is treated as holding a loan on the argument
// Logos: error [fn main]: cannot move out of 'a' because it is borrowed. The `use logos.std.fmt;` import is LOAD-BEARING: without it the same program compiles clean (an import changes a borrowck verdict; an i64-only Item does not reproduce either)
// rustc: compiles and runs, exit 0 — `Item` has no lifetime parameter, so `dup(&a)`'s result carries no loan and `a` may be moved. Reproduced.
// corpus: tests/interactions/clusters/index-clone-keeps-borrow/
// fix hint: borrowck (BIR call-site region flow): a return type that carries no region (bir_type_carries_loans false for a lifetime-free struct with a String field) must not inherit the argument's loans; start from what `use logos.std.fmt` adds that flips the answer for String-carrying types.
package owned_return_from_ref_param_keeps_loan_refused;
use logos.mem.string;
use logos.std.fmt;
use logos.lang.ops;
struct Item { name: String }
fn dup(x: &Item) -> Item { Item { name: x.name.clone() } }
fn main() -> i32 {
    let a = Item { name: String::from("a") };
    let first = dup(&a);
    let owned = a;
    if first.name.len() != 1 || owned.name.len() != 1 { return 3; }
    return 0;
}
